# 1. Use hexagonal architecture

Date: 2026-10-26
Status: Accepted

## Context
The app will get sentences from several sources (Tatoeba, manual entry,
friends, later AI) and will change storage (SQLite now, PostgreSQL later).
These outside systems will change; the learning logic should not.

## Decision
Split the code into three layers inside `src/langex/`:
- `domain/`: core concepts and rules, no external imports
- `application/`: use cases and ports (interfaces such as `SentenceSource`)
- `adapters/`: implementations that talk to the outside world

Dependencies point inward only.

## Consequences
- New sentence sources or databases can be added without changing core logic.
- The domain can be tested quickly without a database or internet.
- More files and folders than a simple script; some extra structure up front.